{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Aaron shall arrange it.</b> Even though the kindling of the lamps, and likewise the daily incense, were valid for generations when performed by an ordinary priest, according to what they of blessed memory received, nevertheless Scripture says regarding both of them \"Aaron.\" For indeed, throughout the days of the wilderness the matter of the Tabernacle was every day like its matter for generations on the Day of Atonement, concerning which it says: כִּי בֶעָנָן אֵרָאֶה עַל הַכַּפֹּרֶת (Leviticus 16:2) — and this is because throughout the days of the wilderness it says: כִּי עֲנַן ה׳ עַל הַמִּשְׁכָּן יוֹמָם וְאֵשׁ תִּהְיֶה לַיְלָה בוֹ וְכוּ׳ (Exodus 40:38). Therefore it was fitting that the acts of the incense and the kindling of the lamps performed inside it be performed by the High Priest, just as they are performed for generations on the Day of Atonement."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:41.198063603Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}